        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Trigger a workflow state transition on an ERP5 document.\n
\n
    Changes the document\'s workflow state (e.g. draft → confirmed → planned).\n
    This is irreversible for most transitions — confirm with the user before calling.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need to change a document\'s state (confirm, validate, cancel, etc.).\n
    - You\'ve verified the action is available via erp5_read\'s \'workflows\' list.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You want to edit field values — use erp5_write instead.\n
    - You want to create a new document — use erp5_create instead.\n
\n
    PREREQUISITE: Call erp5_read first — the \'workflows\' array in the response lists\n
    available actions with their \'name\' values (e.g. \'confirm_action\', \'plan_action\').\n
    </string> </value>
